# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.test" "A macro-body substitution reaches every embedded fence alike, `toml` included"

# `text.html.tiddlywiki5.substitution` keys on `L:meta.variable.macro.body.tiddlywiki5`, an
# ANCESTOR scope: a TextMate injection tests the whole scope path, so a `\define` body's own
# ancestor scope still stands wherever a fence sits inside it — `toml`, `js`, `css`, every
# embedded language alike — and the injection fires inside the fence too. An injection selector's
# `-` exclusion answers only for scopes standing BEFORE its anchor; `meta.embedded.block.toml` and
# `markup.fenced_code.block.tiddlywiki5` both stand AFTER the anchor, deeper in the stack, so
# excluding either leaves the paint unchanged. `toml` reaches exactly as far as every other
# embedded language a `\define` body carries, which is the shared, grammar-wide reach this pins —
# not a scope unique to `toml`. A CONTROL below shows a `\procedure` body carries none of it: the
# injection's own comment states a `\procedure` body never takes text substitution, so nothing
# here answers to `toml` alone.

\define fenced-toml-takes-substitution()
```toml
key = "before $param$ after"
#      ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.embedded.block.toml source.toml.tw5-syntax string.quoted.double.toml
#             ^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 string.quoted.double.toml markup.other.variable.substitute-parameter.tiddlywiki5
```
\end

\procedure fenced-toml-in-a-procedure-body-takes-none()
```toml
key = "before $param$ after"
#      ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.embedded.block.toml source.toml.tw5-syntax string.quoted.double.toml
#             ^^^^^^^ string.quoted.double.toml - markup.other.variable.substitute-parameter.tiddlywiki5
```
\end

```toml
key = "before $param$ after, outside any definition"
#      ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.embedded.block.toml source.toml.tw5-syntax string.quoted.double.toml
#             ^^^^^^^ string.quoted.double.toml - markup.other.variable.substitute-parameter.tiddlywiki5
```
